    <p>Here's the catch I promised. Most "educational" products only push facts at a kid or gamify a lesson, so they do nothing about the one thing that actually went quiet: the wanting to know. Others just dress up a workbook and call it fun. If you buy one of those and your kid never touches it, that isn't the idea of learning at home failing you. That's the wrong tool for the job.</p>

    <p>What worked for us was the approach I keep describing: start with the questions a kid already wonders about, then answer them well enough that they want the next one. That's exactly what the <a href="https://primenaturals.store/products/kids-encyclopedia-100-000-whys" class="vy-vy-dli-product-link">Kid's Encyclopedia 10,000 Whys</a> is built around, with 174 real questions across 6 chapters in one hardcover, for kids ages 6-12. Prime Naturals sells it through its official website, which lets them control quality on every print run and back each order with a 30-day money-back guarantee.</p>

    <p>At the time of writing, first-time customers can claim:</p>

    <ul class="vy-vy-dli-offer-list">
      <li>✅  1 Book for $39.90 (was $79.80), 50% off your first copy, perfect for one child</li>
      <li>✅  Family bundles: 2 Books for $69.90 (extra 25% off), 3 Books for $79.90 (extra 40% off), up to 5 Books for $99.90 (extra 60% off)</li>
      <li>✅  Free shipping and a 30-day money-back guarantee: if it doesn't do for your child what it did for mine, request a full refund. No questions asked.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>Most parents see their kids picking the book up on their own within the first week or two, with deeper questions and steadier focus building from there. The 30-day guarantee matters because it means <span class="vy-vy-dli-bold">you get a full month to see the change before the window closes</span>.</p>

    <a href="https://primenaturals.store/products/kids-encyclopedia-100-000-whys" class="vy-vy-dli-cta-btn">👉 GET THE BOOK »</a>

    <!-- Section 10 -->
    <h2>Why the 10,000 Whys book keeps selling out</h2>

    <div class="vy-vy-dli-image-block">
      <img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/vysta/lp-343-prime-naturals/images/img-9.png" alt="Parents sharing photos of their kids happily reading the 10,000 Whys book">
    </div>

    <p>Since word started spreading, the <a href="https://primenaturals.store/products/kids-encyclopedia-100-000-whys" class="vy-vy-dli-product-link">10,000 Whys</a> book has been getting a lot of attention from parents who are tired of screens and want something that makes their kids want to learn, not just another app. There's also a bottleneck the brand can't rush: each hardcover run is printed and quality-checked before it ships, which limits how fast Prime Naturals can restock when demand spikes.</p>

    <p>If the promotion is still live when you click through, you may still be able to lock in <span class="vy-vy-dli-bold">50% off your first book</span> on the <a href="https://primenaturals.store/products/kids-encyclopedia-100-000-whys" class="vy-vy-dli-product-link">Kid's Encyclopedia 10,000 Whys</a> before the current run sells out.</p>

    <p>I don't usually end articles this way. But after watching my son fall back in love with learning, I'd feel wrong not mentioning that the current pricing won't last.</p>

